<title>USA: Urban Shopping Centers closes refinancing.</title>
<headline>Urban Shopping Centers closes refinancing.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Urban Shopping Centers Inc said Tuesday it recently completed a $170-million debt refinancing for the Water Tower Place retail/office project in Chicago.</p>
<p>The property is 55-percent owned by Urban Shopping Centers and an institutional investment group owns the other 45 percent stake, the real estate investment trust said.</p>
<p>The new loan matures on February 1, 1999, Urban Shopping Centers said.</p>
<p>The company's shares were off 1/8 Tuesday at 30-1/4.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
